1
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,080
Hey, you guys.

2
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:07,670
Hey.

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:07,670
What are you doing?

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,960
Figuring out our wedding plans.

5
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,960
We were doing the same thing.

6
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:12,630
Yeah.

7
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:17,300
It's really crazy. The hall, the dress, the food.

8
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:20,890
I had no idea how expensive this stuff was.

9
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:20,890
Yeah, it is really pricey.

10
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:24,600
I freaked when I heard the numbers.

11
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:24,600
So, what did you two do about it?

12
00:00:24,770 --> 00:00:27,690
It was simple. I came up with some cost-cutting solutions...

13
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:30,860
...wrote out a list and Monica told me to go to hell.

14
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:33,650
There's no way around it.

15
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:36,570
Just accept that this is gonna cost a lot of money.

16
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:40,200
I heard that weddings are, like, a $40 billion-a-year industry.

17
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:43,370
Yeah. And I'm responsible for just, like, half of that.

18
00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:48,420
But really, it does seem like this money could be put to better use.

19
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:49,670
Are you serious?

20
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:53,170
Yeah. Now, how would you feel if we gave all the wedding money to charity...

21
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:55,720
...and we just got married at City Hall?

22
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,180
I think it would make me wanna marry you even more.

23
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:04,220
Well, I gotta say, you guys, that's an incredible gesture.

24
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:06,390
Maybe you do that next time you get married.

25
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:12,610
No, no, no. The next time's gonna be Hawaii at sunset.

26
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,740
But maybe the time after that.

27
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:57,150
Hey.

28
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:57,150
Hey.

29
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,400
What's going on?

30
00:01:58,570 --> 00:02:02,200
Our adoption social worker is coming by, so we're cleaning the apartment.

31
00:02:02,450 --> 00:02:04,080
"We"?

32
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:08,660
You know you don't want me to help. You can't have it both ways.

33
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,920
Hey, is this the person who decides whether or not you get a baby?

34
00:02:13,090 --> 00:02:16,460
Kind of. She's coming to see where we live.

35
00:02:13,090 --> 00:02:16,460
And it has to go perfectly.

36
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:21,010
If she doesn't like us, she can keep us off every adoption list in the state.

37
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:24,390
Hey, maybe I should stop by. She could be a soap-opera fan.

38
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:28,020
It's very impressive when the little people know a celebrity.

39
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:30,350
"Little people"?

40
00:02:30,770 --> 00:02:32,310
"Celebrity."

41
00:02:33,730 --> 00:02:35,480
So I think I'm just about done here.

42
00:02:35,650 --> 00:02:40,360
Unless you have any bad stuff hidden somewhere, like porn or cigarettes?

43
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:42,240
What?

44
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:46,120
No.

45
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:46,120
Chandler.

46
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:52,540
I don't, and I'm offended by the insinuation.

47
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:55,340
So there's not a magazine under the couch...

48
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:58,510
...or a pack of cigarettes taped to the back of the toilet tank...

49
00:02:58,670 --> 00:03:01,220
...or a filthy video in the VCR?

50
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:04,090
I'll admit to the cigarettes and the magazine.

51
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:05,850
But that tape is not mine.

52
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:10,100
It isn't mine.

53
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:10,100
I guess we'll never know whose it is.

54
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:19,190
May I help you?

55
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:19,190
Yes.

56
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:22,610
We're here to make a rather sizable donation to the children.

57
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:25,410
Well, any contribution, large or small, is appreciated.

58
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:28,700
Well, I think you're gonna appreciate the crap out of this one.

59
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:32,330
Well, this is very generous.

60
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:32,330
And we don't want any recognition.

61
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,170
This is completely anonymous.

62
00:03:34,330 --> 00:03:36,920
Completely anonymous. From two kind strangers.

63
00:03:37,090 --> 00:03:40,130
Mr. X and Phoebe Buffay.

64
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:43,180
We can put your names in our newsletter.

65
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,260
Not necessary.

66
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,260
Buffay is spelled B-U-F-F-A-Y.

67
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:51,520
And X is spelled, uh, "Mike Hannigan."

68
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:55,350
All right, well, on behalf of the children, thank you both very much.

69
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:59,860
Sure. I'm glad we did this. It feels so good.

70
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:59,860
It does. It feels really good.

71
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:02,610
Oh, look. And we get these free T-shirts.

72
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:06,030
Actually, that's the shirt I wore to the gym.

73
00:04:06,410 --> 00:04:07,990
It's moist.

74
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,830
Emma will be up in a minute.

75
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,830
Oh, good.

76
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,420
Oh, hey, Ross, listen. I heard about you and Charlie. I'm really sorry.

77
00:04:18,590 --> 00:04:22,800
Aw, that's okay. I'm sure there are tons of other beautiful paleontologists out there.

78
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:25,760
Absolutely.

79
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:25,760
There was one. She's it.

80
00:04:25,930 --> 00:04:29,140
All the rest look like they should live under a bridge.

81
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:33,270
So, uh, what are you gonna do today?

82
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:35,890
Well, I was thinking of taking Emma to the playground.

83
00:04:36,230 --> 00:04:38,610
Oh, my God. What?

84
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:44,780
Like I said, I was thinking of taking Emma to the Museum of Knives and Fire.

85
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:53,040
Okay, look, Ross. I do not want Emma going to the playground.

86
00:04:56,250 --> 00:04:57,460
Because?

87
00:04:57,630 --> 00:05:01,380
All right, if you must know, I had a traumatic...

88
00:05:01,550 --> 00:05:05,170
...swing incident when I was little.

89
00:05:06,050 --> 00:05:08,010
Seriously?

90
00:05:06,050 --> 00:05:08,010
Yes. I was 4 years old.

91
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:10,010
And I was on the swing...

92
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:14,020
...and then all of a sudden my hair got tangled in the chain.

93
00:05:15,890 --> 00:05:20,770
And to get me out, my mom had to cut a big chunk of my hair.

94
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:24,110
And it was uneven for weeks.

95
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:33,490
And you made it through that?

96
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:38,000
I wonder who's gonna play you in the movie.

97
00:05:39,290 --> 00:05:43,170
Okay, fine, you can make fun of me. I do not want Emma going there.

98
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:45,960
And I was thinking Claire Danes.

99
00:05:46,970 --> 00:05:49,430
Look, I'm sorry to hear about your tragedy.

100
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:53,390
Okay? But the swings are perfectly safe. And besides, Emma loves them.

101
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:58,560
You should come, and you'll see.

102
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:58,560
Those things go, like, 40 miles an hour.

103
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:01,060
And there's that moment when you're at the top...

104
00:06:01,230 --> 00:06:05,070
...when you just don't know if you're gonna return back to Earth.

105
00:06:06,650 --> 00:06:09,610
Space is filled with orbiting children.

106
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:14,790
Look, please, just come on.

107
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:18,620
When you see the look on Emma's face, I swear, you won't regret it.

108
00:06:21,290 --> 00:06:22,750
All right.

109
00:06:21,290 --> 00:06:22,750
Good.

110
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,380
You don't wanna be a mothers...

111
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:27,760
...who pass on their irrational fears to their children, do you?

112
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:29,380
"Irrational," huh?

113
00:06:29,550 --> 00:06:33,300
I'll remember that next time you freak out about a spider in your apartment.

114
00:06:33,470 --> 00:06:34,550
Oh, yeah, that's the same.

115
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:37,770
I'm sure there are 30 different species of poisonous swings.

116
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:44,150
Oh, my God. The adoption lady is early.

117
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,070
Okay. Okay. Here we go.

118
00:06:46,230 --> 00:06:47,650
Okay.

119
00:06:46,230 --> 00:06:47,650
Here we go.

120
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:49,070
Stand up straight.

121
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,070
Big smile.

122
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:56,490
Hello. Is this the Creepy residence?

123
00:06:56,660 --> 00:07:00,080
We're waiting for the adoption lady. But, hey, I'm glad you're here.

124
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:02,790
I was cleaning this morning and I found this.

125
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:06,000
I don't know if you wanna use it, but...

126
00:07:06,170 --> 00:07:09,260
Oh, this is so sweet of you.

127
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:13,220
Oh, but I won't be needing a veil. I actually won't be wearing a dress at all.

128
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:16,350
I told you, I am not coming to a naked wedding.

129
00:07:16,510 --> 00:07:18,810
No, no, no. We're not having a big reception.

130
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,850
We took the wedding money we were gonna spend...

131
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:22,890
...and donated it to a children's charity.

132
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:24,690
That's crazy!

133
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:30,990
I'm sorry. I can't imagine giving up my one wedding day like that.

134
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:34,490
Yeah, well, we're different. I don't care about having a huge party.

135
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:36,950
This is really nice for you, but...

136
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:40,700
Oh, please. I put this on and, ugh, I just look like...

137
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,750
Well, radiant.

138
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:49,000
All right, but who cares? You know, I don't need a pretty veil and a fancy dress.

139
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:51,170
That's right. You're making a commitment.

140
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:54,840
And, you know, that's the same whether you do it at the Plaza or...

141
00:07:55,010 --> 00:07:56,930
Where you gonna do it?

142
00:07:55,010 --> 00:07:56,930
City Hall.

143
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:58,600
Oh!

144
00:07:58,810 --> 00:08:01,730
Oh, that sounds nice.

145
00:08:01,890 --> 00:08:06,150
I was just there for jury duty. They've really spruced that place up.

146
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:10,940
Okay. No, it's okay. It's okay. It's okay. I've made my decision.

147
00:08:11,110 --> 00:08:13,860
What I really want is a great big wedding.

148
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,950
Yay!

149
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:20,660
But you gave all the money to charity.

150
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:20,660
Well, I'll just ask for it back.

151
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:24,290
I don't think you can do that.

152
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:24,290
Why not?

153
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:28,750
This is her wedding day. That's way more important than some stupid kids.

154
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:33,420
That's sweet, honey, but save something for the adoption lady.

155
00:08:40,010 --> 00:08:42,850
All right, okay. Be careful.

156
00:08:40,010 --> 00:08:42,850
Okay.

157
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:46,390
Careful. Watch her hair. Watch her hair!

158
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:50,230
Rach, she's got, like, three hairs.

159
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:50,230
I know. I know.

160
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:55,610
But they're just so beautiful. Oh, my God, I just pulled one out.

161
00:08:55,780 --> 00:08:59,320
I promise you she's safe, okay? Watch how much she loves this.

162
00:08:59,490 --> 00:09:03,160
Okay. Okay.

163
00:08:59,490 --> 00:09:03,160
Are you ready, sweetie? Here we go.

164
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:09,000
Okay, careful. Okay. Oh.

165
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,340
She's smiling.

166
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:15,920
Look at that, she does like it.

167
00:09:16,090 --> 00:09:19,510
See, I told you.

168
00:09:16,090 --> 00:09:19,510
Oh. Ah!

169
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:26,730
Oh, my God. Look at her, she's a little daredevil.

170
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:29,980
Oh, God. Let me push. Can I push?

171
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:29,980
Oh, absolutely.

172
00:09:30,150 --> 00:09:34,820
Okay. Oh, God. Okay, get the camera. It's in the diaper bag.

173
00:09:34,990 --> 00:09:36,400
Okay.

174
00:09:36,570 --> 00:09:41,780
See? Scared of the swings. I bet you feel pretty silly. Aah!

175
00:09:45,790 --> 00:09:47,830
We're seriously asking for the money back?

176
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,540
It's for our wedding day.

177
00:09:49,710 --> 00:09:53,880
All right, now, is this guy gay or straight? Because one of us has to start flirting.

178
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:57,380
Wow. You here to make another donation the same day?

179
00:09:57,550 --> 00:09:59,630
I don't think that's ever happened before.

180
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,510
Gay. Go.

181
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:07,310
Oh, my God, I love your shirt.

182
00:10:08,810 --> 00:10:13,360
The donation we made earlier? Um, well, we want it back.

183
00:10:14,610 --> 00:10:15,690
Excuse me?

184
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:19,360
See, okay, that money was for a big wedding we thought we didn't want.

185
00:10:19,530 --> 00:10:21,360
But it turns out we do.

186
00:10:21,530 --> 00:10:24,620
So you're asking us to refund your donation to the children?

187
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,540
Yeah.

188
00:10:27,830 --> 00:10:30,170
This feels really good.

189
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:37,340
Yeah, I'm sorry. I am. But this wedding's just really important to me.

190
00:10:37,510 --> 00:10:41,180
Hey, it's none of my business. Besides, this is probably a good thing.

191
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:45,970
We've really been spoiling the children, what with all the food and warm clothing.

192
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:49,680
That's not fair. A person's wedding is important.

193
00:10:49,850 --> 00:10:51,480
And especially to me.

194
00:10:51,650 --> 00:10:55,440
Okay, I didn't have a graduation party. And I didn't go to prom.

195
00:10:55,610 --> 00:10:59,360
And I spent my sweet 16 being chased around a tire yard...

196
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:03,200
...by an escaped mental patient who, in his own words, wanted to:

197
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:05,030
"Kill me, or whatever."

198
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:09,580
So I deserve a real celebration.

199
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:14,130
And I'm not gonna let some sweaty little man make me feel badly about it.

200
00:11:18,590 --> 00:11:21,260
She could've been talking about either one of us.

201
00:11:27,430 --> 00:11:30,390
Hi, I'm Laura. I'm here for your adoption interview.

202
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:33,190
Hi, I'm Monica. And this is Chandler.

203
00:11:33,350 --> 00:11:35,560
Hi. Thank you.

204
00:11:33,350 --> 00:11:35,560
Please come in.

205
00:11:35,730 --> 00:11:38,780
Would you like something to drink?

206
00:11:35,730 --> 00:11:38,780
Water would be fine.

207
00:11:38,940 --> 00:11:41,110
We're so glad that you're here.

208
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:43,910
We're really excited about getting this process started.

209
00:11:44,070 --> 00:11:47,080
Because we love kids. Love them to death.

210
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:50,660
Well, not actually to death. That's just a figure of speech.

211
00:11:50,830 --> 00:11:53,040
We love kids the appropriate amount...

212
00:11:54,710 --> 00:11:57,000
...as allowed by law.

213
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:01,130
Your place is just lovely.

214
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:01,130
Thank you.

215
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:05,300
Yes, this building does have a wholesome, family feel to it.

216
00:12:05,470 --> 00:12:07,760
I feel like I've been here before.

217
00:12:07,930 --> 00:12:09,930
Are any other couples in the building adopting?

218
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,930
Is that that couple on the first floor?

219
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:14,480
Because we should get a baby before them.

220
00:12:14,650 --> 00:12:16,520
That guy tried to sell me drugs.

221
00:12:18,150 --> 00:12:21,610
But other than that, wholesome, wholesome building.

222
00:12:22,490 --> 00:12:23,860
Oh.

223
00:12:24,030 --> 00:12:27,530
What?

224
00:12:24,030 --> 00:12:27,530
I just realized why I remember this place.

225
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:29,870
Really? What is it?

226
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:29,870
Oh, it's nothing.

227
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:34,330
I went on a date with a guy who lived in this building. It didn't end very well.

228
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:37,460
That wouldn't, by any chance, be Joey Tribbiani?

229
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:40,590
Yes!

230
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:40,590
Of course it was.

231
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:45,760
We had a great night. In the morning, he promised he'd call and he didn't.

232
00:12:45,930 --> 00:12:47,430
Rat bastard!

233
00:12:49,470 --> 00:12:52,100
So you're not friends with him?

234
00:12:49,470 --> 00:12:52,100
Oh, God, no.

235
00:12:52,270 --> 00:12:54,430
No, no, no.

236
00:12:52,270 --> 00:12:54,430
No. Nope.

237
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:58,520
No, no, no.

238
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:58,520
No, no, no. No.

239
00:12:58,690 --> 00:13:00,230
No.

240
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:04,320
Well, I'm sorry I brought it up.

241
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:07,030
So are either one of you planning on staying at home?

242
00:13:08,410 --> 00:13:12,620
Hello? Anybody in there order a celebrity?

243
00:13:12,870 --> 00:13:14,750
Ow!

244
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,250
What was that?

245
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:21,040
That's just some crazy guy who roams the halls here.

246
00:13:21,210 --> 00:13:23,090
He's great with kids, though.

247
00:13:30,550 --> 00:13:34,350
Ross. Oh, my God, are you okay?

248
00:13:30,550 --> 00:13:34,350
Son of a bitch!

249
00:13:38,270 --> 00:13:40,940
Oh, relax. I didn't say the F-word.

250
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:46,030
Ross, see, I told you! Those swings are evil!

251
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,280
All right. That is it.

252
00:13:47,450 --> 00:13:51,120
That's the last time Emma is getting on one of those things for her entire life.

253
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:54,870
No, no, no. Okay, it wasn't the swing's fault. It was my fault.

254
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:58,080
And kind of that kid's fault.

255
00:13:58,290 --> 00:14:01,250
Who is still laughing. Nice.

256
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:05,000
